  "term": "sensitive soul",
  "definition": "In historical philosophy and psychology, the sensitive soul was a lower kind of soul distinguished from the rational soul. In the passage, it is treated, along with the vegetative soul, as a preparatory form in the embryo rather than the form that specifically makes a human being human.",
